    "This file is a non-executable reference policy; actual provider JSON is generated only in the corpus-generation environment.",
    "The preferred Stage A baseline separates license evidence, training-model provenance, and runnable release assets instead of claiming that all three come from one file tree.",
    "The Apache-2.0 model-card is pinned independently from the sherpa-onnx release archive used at runtime.",
    "The sherpa release archive checksum is corroborated by two independent downstream integrity manifests because the upstream GitHub release asset does not publish a digest; local generation remains fail-closed on the pinned archive size and SHA-256.",
    "No binary equality is assumed between the HF training ONNX and the sherpa release model.onnx.",
    "The resampling profile hash-binds the Python adapter, TTS backend executable, resampler executable, model, tokens, lexicon, license evidence, and verified runtime-asset receipt.",
